@0    = ~You've been quiet as of late, <CHARNAME>, what's on your mind?~
@1    = ~I was wondering about your comment to Irenicus in Spellhold. You called him a "traitor". What did you mean by that? It's almost like you know him.~
@2    = ~I consider him a traitor to The Weave and surface elves. He uses magic for his own evil deeds and that to me, is intolerable. People of this nature need to be put to the sword.~
@3    = ~I understand how you feel about the abuses of the magical Weave but how could you tell he was an elf? I could not tell what he was.~
@4    = ~Not that I question Gorion's upbringing of you, <CHARNAME>, but if you were raised by elves, then you would recognize one of our own. But that's beside the point, we have to put an end to Irenicus and his schemes. He is far too dangerous to be left unchecked.~
@5    = ~That sounds sensible enough. Irenicus has done great harm to everyone and everything he touches. We should get going and find Irenicus.~
@6    = ~We elves can "sense" another elf, even if they are disguised by magical means. But that's besides the point, we have to put an end to Irenicus and his schemes. He is far too dangerous to be left unchecked.~
@7    = ~Yes we should. I have a feeling we have a long hard road ahead of us, before we meet Irenicus again.~
@8    = ~I find looking like a drow revolting, <CHARNAME>. Looking like an elf's most vile and evil enemy is beyond words to describe.~
@9    = ~I know its uneasy for you Nina but we have to do this so we can get to Irenicus.~
@10   = ~Please quit crying over it Nina. You are in my party and do what I command.~
@11   = ~I know I just wish there was another way to do it. This makes me so uneasy, wearing the skin of my enemy. I'll adapt to it I suppose.~
@12   = ~I, for one thing am not "crying" over it, but expressing how I feel. Since it is obvious you do not give a damn I'll remain silent for the brief time I am in this group.~
@13   = ~(In a low whispering voice.) My skin just crawls being in this hell hole, <CHARNAME>. I hope our stay here is brief. Being in a city of an elf's most hated enemy is unbearable.~
@14   = ~Well Nina you must do this for us. The only way we are going to find Irenicus is by searching for answers here.~
@15   = ~Please Nina keep these kinds of comments to yourself. We may be whispering but what if these drow can read lips?~
@16   = ~Yes, you are correct, <CHARNAME>. I just hope we find the answers quickly and be done with this cess pit.~
@17   = ~Ohh. That's right some drow specialize in silent communication in sign language or lip reading. I hope we find the answers quickly and be done with this cess pit.~
@18   = ~I have seen you in action, <CHARNAME> and I must say your spell casting is quite good. Who taught you the ways of a mage?~
@19   = ~My foster father, Gorion, taught me. We would spends hours a day going over the scrolls so I could memorize the spell just right. It took me a while but I would get the spell memorized and cast it to Gorion's expectations.~
@20   = ~I am self taught actually.~
@21   = ~I do not want to talk about this right now.~
@22   = ~It sounds like Gorion was a stern task master. My uncle was stern at times. He would make me write down the scroll word for word fifty times until I got it right. I learned very quick doing it that way.~
@23   = ~I can imagine. writing down a scroll that many times, I bet you could recite it in your sleep.~
@24   = ~Interesting Nina. We should get going.~
@25   = ~Not quickly enough. I learned a spell far quicker then what you described Nina.~
@26   = ~Self taught? Surely you jest. Learning the ways of magic is hard enough with a teacher, but by yourself?~
@27   = ~Ha ha I just wanted to see that surprised look on your face, Nina. Actually my foster father, Gorion, taught me. We would spends hours a day going over the scrolls so I could memorize the spell just right. It took me a while but I would get the spell memorized and cast it to Gorions expectations.~
@28   = ~Very well some other time perhaps?~
@29   = ~Yes I could and it would give me nightmares for days! He he. Well enough talk on this for now, perhaps more later on.~
@30   = ~I am sure you did master wizard. I bet you could run circles around Elminster himself. (Nina rolls her eyes at you.) Mayhaps your grand mastery could teach me something? Then again perhaps not. Lets go.~
@31   = ~I have seen you in action, <CHARNAME>, and I must say your fighting style is quite good. Who taught you in the martial ways?~
@32   = ~I learned a lot from Jondalar and the guards at Candlekeep. I also learned from my travels on the road, fighting brigands, highway men and thieves.~
@33   = ~Being on the road? Yes, I would guess that one would pick up things rather quickly, the roads of the Swordcoast are fraught with highwaymen and brigands.~
@34   = ~I am curious, where did you learn your sword fighting from?~
@35   = ~They are indeed. Lets get going.~
@36   = ~Yes that is very true. It seemed like every time we left a town, we would encounter some pathetic rag tag band of thieves looking for a quick score. You seem good with a sword Nina, who taught you?~
@37   = ~My uncle taught me some of the aspects of sword fighting, mostly if it dealt with casting spells and sword fighting. Most of the knowledge in fighting I learned from Tantharin a master elven swordsmen. I was apprenticed to him at an early age. He was a very hard taskmaster, if not brutal sometimes. (Nina brushes her hair back by her right ear to reveal a small scar that leads from her ear towards the back of her head.) See this?~
@38   = ~Yes. Did he do that to you?~
@39   = ~Yes he did. It was a valuable lesson that was taught. I was becoming very good with the sword, or so I thought, that I was starting to become cocky with the other students. Tantharin saw this and decided it was time for me to advance up the next level in sword fighting. I failed his advance level within moments. Before I even had a chance to defend myself, he moved so quickly at me that with one swift swing he cut half of my hair off, left this scar, then knocked me on the ground and before I knew it, had his sword at my throat. He said, "Are you still confident in your 'master' abilities with a sword?"~
@40   = ~The lesson I learned was, being overconfident and thinking of yourself as being above others will leave you open for attack and defeat. Such thinking will lead you to underestimate your enemy as Tantharin showed me.~
@41   = ~A good lesson to learn but he could have taught you a different way then leave a scar on you.~
@42   = ~Bah you were weak! I would have taught him a lesson in leaving scars on me.~
@43   = ~Perhaps, but that was his way. He said a small scar from a lesson learned and understood was a small price to pay than having your head severed from your body in an actual fight.~
@44   = ~You're such an arrogant <PRO_RACE>, I would have loved to see Tantharin teach you a lesson or two!~
@45   = ~You have done good deeds in Baldur's Gate, <CHARNAME>, but now you act as if those good deeds mean nothing. Do not slip into the ways of evil my friend.~
@46   = ~Quit harassing me already Nina I do not need it. Better yet, mind your own business.~
@47   = ~You are right Nina and I will try to do what is best. I will not stray again.~
@48   = ~I am sorry to see your attitude has moved into the negative like our enemies. This is my business since me and others are affected by your actions. I shall be watching you very closely <CHARNAME>.~
@49   = ~You speak sincerely now but your actions will show how sincere you really are. We shall see if your actions match your words and if true then things will be well with me.~
@50   = ~Very well, <CHARNAME>, anything you wish I will do. Just keep him away from me and we shall get along fine.~
@51   = ~Good. Now that everyone is getting along, lets move out.~
@52   = ~<CHARNAME>, I noticed you and Anomen have been getting close lately. Are you... are you two starting a serious relationship?~
@53   = ~That is a straight forward question you have Nina and one that is really not of your concern.~
@54   = ~Me and Anomen? Oh please! We're just good friends that is all.~
@55   = ~Anomen? You could say we are, I'm growing quite fond of him.~
@56   = ~Not of my concern? Of course its my concern, he's been sweet talking me for a while and if he's starting to get involved with you, well there's going to be some hard choices made right now!~
@57   = ~You're giving me an ultimatum? Well listen hear sister, if you don't like my involvement with Anomen, you are free to leave!~
@58   = ~Why are you getting mad Nina? If you're going to be this way about it, I'll answer the question and the answer is we are not starting a serious relationship, we're just friends.~
@59   = ~Well if you're going to get mad about this, fine I'll answer your question. Over the time we've been together I've grown quite fond of Anomen. Why?~
@60   = ~Fine I will! (Ninafer give <CHARNAME> and Anomen a dirty look and then leaves.)~
@61   = ~You are? Oh, well when I saw you two being around each other a lot lately, I thought, well it's nothing. Forget I ever brought this up.~
@62   = ~You are fond him? Oh I guess... well I hope it works out for you two.~
@63   = ~Aerie my dear, it pleases me that you use magic for the greater good. For someone who has had a traumatic past, you have a positive outlook on life that is quite refreshing.~
@64   = ~T-thank you for saying that Nina. I think magic should be used to help people out and only used for defensive purposes. I-I do not let my past influence me in a negative way. If I did, then those who did me harm would win and I w-would be no better then them. But I do miss my wings though...~
@65   = ~I am sorry about your wings, it is unfortunate that there is no spell that could restore them. It may be hard to live without them but what is done is done. You must accept this and move ahead Aerie. Dwelling in the past with the "what ifs" will not help you.~
@66   = ~I k-know you mean well Nina but it's n-not that easy.~
@67   = ~Life is not easy my friend. Be strong and live that's all I ask.~
@68   = ~I-I will try Nina a-and I thank you for caring.~
@69   = ~You are welcome, we shall chat more on this later.~
@70   = ~The forest at last! Ahh, I am never quite so happy as when I am in the wildest parts of nature. I am always at home here. See the Wood Ferns, the Toad Mushrooms and the Rail Birds in all of their glory! I wonder Nina, being an elf, do you love nature like myself?~
@71   = ~I was raised in the forests. I love walking in the woods and observing the life there. My uncle taught me herbal lore and the benefits of using herbs for healing. See the Grey Lined Oak? When you have the right mixture of leaves with Ganges Root juice, it creates a jell that can be used to close wounds quickly and cleanly.~
@72   = ~That is true Nina, but when it is not mixed just right, it creates a nonfatal poison to the body. The constant vomiting and sleepless nights is something to remember.~
@73   = ~It sounds like Cernd, that you made that mistake.~
@74   = ~One will learn their lesson well and never forget it if they make a mistake like that. Indeed I made that mistake and I recall that week in detail. I had very little sleep and not able to keep much of anything down.~
@75   = ~I know what you mean, it took me three attempts before I got it just right.~
@76   = ~Why does thou look at me with an evil eye? Have I done something to offend you? (As if I care.)~
@77   = ~You are a mage, one that uses magic for his own personal evil ways. You are an enemy of my Goddess and myself.~
@78   = ~I have many enemies, you being one of them means nothing to me. I would destroy you like one does with the crushing a fly.~
@79   = ~Such typical Thayvian arrogance. I would have expected nothing less from an evil mage with dreams of grandeur who will never get anywhere in life, except an early grave.~
@80   = ~Is that all you have to offer? (I am surely not impressed with this twit and her childish taunts.) I should have expect this type of response from an inferior elf. Begone from my sight fool.~
@81   = ~Be careful in battle, Thayvian scourge, you never know when a fireball may go astray and hit you.~
@82   = ~The same could be said to you. One never knows when a spell may hit another target. (It would be a shame if an imprisonment spell struck you.)~
@83   = ~You're an oddity Haer Dalis'. I do not mean that in an offense, I never met a tiefling before.~
@84   = ~Tieflings do not frequent here much my canary. 'Tis a shame though, for this world is fascinating.~
@85   = ~Is it true that tieflings have the blood of demons in them?~
@86   = ~True that we do, but not get the wrong impression. We are not all evil, we are the same as anyone else.~
@87   = ~I am sure tieflings are. I was curious, that is all.~
@88   = ~If you wish to know more of my people, you may ask, my canary.~
@89   = ~Hey Imoen I am so glad we rescued you from Irenicus. Being in Spellhold must have been hell.~
@90   = ~Thanks Ninafer. It was hell being in there. Come to think of it we did have some fun when we could get around the guards. I played a joke on Dradeel by taking one of his recipe books and hid it in Tiax's room. Dradeel went on ranting about some doggies stealing his book until he saw Tiax reading it. Dradeel went into Tiax's room and snatched the book out of his hands. Then Tiax said "No one walks into Tiax's divine room without his say so. Get out before Tiax smites thee!" Then they started to get into a pushing match.~
@91   = ~Did they get into a fist fight?~
@92   = ~No I didn't let it get that far. I went in there and confessed at what I did. Then they both started to chew me out good! The nerve of those two! They chewed me out after I saved them from beating each other to a pulp. Heh.~
@93   = ~Ha ha! Your humor never ceases to amaze me Imoen. Just make sure you keep your sticky fingers and pranks from me.~
@94   = ~Don't tell me you have no sense of humor Nina.~
@95   = ~Indeed I have one. While we were talking I took the liberty of taking your food pouch from you.~
@96   = ~Hey you! Gimme my pouch back!~
@97   = ~Not until I get some of those chocolates you have stashed in there.~
@98   = ~Ok you can have one chocolate and that's because you pulled a fast one on me. Even <CHARNAME> hasn't been able to do that.~
@99   = ~A well learned lesson for you Imoen, divert your targets attention from your goal and you can catch them unaware. A good lesson in battle to.~
@100  = ~You mean like taking your dagger?~
@101  = ~Hey!~
@102  = ~See I learn quickly. Ha ha!~
@103  = ~It is good to be back in the outdoors again. The fresh air is relaxing and soothes the body.~
@104  = ~Yes it does. This reminds me of Su.. I mean my home. It was in the forest with huge trees and watchful squirrels. We elves are at home here.~
@105  = ~True enough, Ninafer. Perhaps some day I will return to the woods when my adventures with <CHARNAME> is over.~
@106  = ~Maybe I will when age and my use as a defender of law and right is over, I will return to what was once my home. But that will not be for some time. I have a duty to perform and luxury’s as this can not be in my life right now.~
@107  = ~I think we have reminisced enough on things that are not possible in our lives at the moment. Lets carry on shall we?~
@108  = ~Jaheira, I was wondering how long have you known <CHARNAME>. How did the two of you meet?~
@109  = ~I've known <PRO_HIMHER> for a while. Me and Khalid met <CHARNAME> at the Friendly Arm Inn. We were friends of Gorian and agreed to help <CHARNAME> in the event of Gorian's death. We did many deeds including bring down Sarevok in Baldur's Gate.~
@110  = ~Sarevok was <PRO_HISHER> half brother right?~
@111  = ~Yes he was. Sarevok was trying to reclaim his father's godhood. It was a tough fight with him and his friends but we prevailed. Why are you asking these questions Nina?~
@112  = ~I was just wondering about what <CHARNAME> has gone through in <PRO_HISHER> life since leaving Candlekeep. I've heard of some stories about what went on in Baldur's Gate. I would prefer hearing such things from someone who has been there than a second hand source.~
@113  = ~I agree with you on that. I prefer to know the truthful facts of a matter myself.~
@114  = ~Is it true that war between Amn and Baldur's Gate never happened thanks to <CHARNAME> and friends?~
@115  = ~Yes we were responsible for that. When the truth about the Iron Throne and Sarevok's manipulations came out, both cities started to be on socialable terms again.~
@116  = ~I am truly in awe at what has been accomplished and the help you gave to those in need. I am honored to be in this group Jaheira. Truly I am. I have more questions to ask but I will ask them at another time.~
@117  = ~Very well lets get going.~
@118  = ~Jaheira, I noticed you still wear your marriage ring around your finger.~
@119  = ~What do you mean by that?~
@120  = ~I find it honorable that you remember Khalid by wearing the ring, that is all.~
@121  = ~He will always be in my heart... always. I-I prefer not to talk about him now Nina.~
@122  = ~Lady Ninafer, you handle the sword like an age old master but you look so young. Where did you learn your sword skills from?~
@123  = ~So young Sir Keldorn? You make me blush with that comment. I learn how to use a sword at a very young age when I was first able to lift a sword up. My uncle was a swordsmith and weapon master. He taught me everything about sword fighting plus cast spells at the same time, which is not very easy to do. It took me many years just to cast a simple spell while fighting.~
@124  = ~It takes discipline, many years of discipline to accomplish that kind of feat. As a squire I was taught how to master the sword and learn the duties of a knight in the Order.~
@125  = ~I have heard of Most Noble Order of the Radiant Heart. They have the most noble and honorable knights that I have encountered. I am glad you are in our party Keldorn.~
@126  = ~Thank you for the kind words, Lady Ninafer.~
@127  = ~You are welcome Sir. I may not belong to a noble order but I strive to bring nobility and justice to those who practice magic through the magical Weave of Mystra. Those who abuse the gift of Mystra are the bane to those of us who practice magic. Justice must be dealt to those who practice magic for evil.~
@128  = ~A just cause indeed, Lady Ninafer, to serve one's god.~
@129  = ~It is indeed, Keldorn.~
@130  = ~We should talk more of this Nina in a more relaxed atmosphere. There is much in common we have to discuss.~
@131  = ~Korgan it is beyond me why <CHARNAME> has such a vile evil creature in <PRO_HISHER> party. Step out of line and I'll send you to whatever gods would take your filthy soul.~
@132  = ~Eh what's this? Ye be sayin that with such love behind it sweety. Mayhaps we go some where private and talk more about this?~
@133  = ~The only place private we will be going dwarf is some where no one will see me run my sword through that fat belly of yours.~
@134  = ~I thought we would 'ave started somethin romantic but ye got personal by callin me fat. Ye damned longed limbed fey elf, ye keep them insults commin and yer head and me axe be meetin.~
@135  = ~See it just goes to prove my point that you are evil and unthinking on top of it. Someone insults you and the first thing you think about is killing them. Pathetic.~
@136  = ~Well I ain't impressed by ya either, fey elf. Why don't ye keep yer distance from me, go find some bloody trees and dance around 'em.~
@137  = ~I will keep my distance but I will also keep an eye on you.~
@138  = ~Ye bloody wench, yer aim with that magic done hit me! Watch it next time!~
@139  = ~*My* aim? There is nothing wrong with my aim dwarf. If that fat body of yours jumps in the way of my target after I cast the spell, there is nothing I can do to stop it.~
@140  = ~Fat ye say? This ain't fat ya stupid fey elf, it's pure dwarven muscle! I think ye be itchin fer me to use it on ye. What say you?~
@141  = ~You amuse me little one with your bluster and bravado. You would not be able to get an arms length near me before I cut you down.~
@142  = ~Well lets put it to a test aye?~
@143  = ~Indeed, why don't we.~
@144  = ~Ninafer, I am curious if you are a knight to any order?~
@145  = ~In a manner of speaking I am a knight to Mystra, but I do not belong to any special orders. I make sure that magic is not abused and vilified by evil beings. My Goddess does not like The Weave to be abused in such a way, but she can not really do anything about in sake of the other gods. But it does not rule out Her worshippers from stopping the evil doers from abusing magic. I have pledge my life and soul to Her and the protection of The Weave. So yes Mazzy I am a knight but only to my Goddess.~
@146  = ~That is very noble of you, Ninafer.~
@147  = ~You may call me Nina. All people that are my friends call me Nina.~
@148  = ~Why thank you, Nina.~
@149  = ~Your patron God is Arvoreen correct? I am afraid I do not know much about Him. Could you tell me about Him?~
@150  = ~Arvoreen is a noble and vigilant god of the halflings. He is also known as The Defender because he defends all that is right and good and destroys those who are evil. He is the warrior god of us halfling that inspires us to do what is right in our lives.~
@151  = ~I see we have a lot in common Mazzy. It looks like we shall get along great. Lets get going, it appears <CHARNAME> wants us to hurry up.~
@152  = ~Minsc, where is that little rodent of yours?.~
@153  = ~Rodent? You mean Boo? Boo is no rodent no siree. Boo is a mighty space hamster! He is right here in my pocket. Hmmm.~
@154  = ~Hmmm what Minsc?~
@155  = ~Boo is not in my pocket. Minsc does not know where Boo has gone.~
@156  = ~Well that is because he is in my pouch of food again Minsc! Why is it he is always raiding my food stuff instead of yours?~
@157  = ~Oh Boo you got Minsc in trouble once again! Come here..~
@158  = ~Not so fast, Minsc, you did not answer my question. Why is Boo raiding my food and not yours?~
@159  = ~Little elf lady should not be holding Boo away from Minsc! It is most unwise!~
@160  = ~MINSC! Would you answer the question.~
@161  = ~Minsc does not know why.~
@162  = ~Well I think I know why Minsc. My food is fresh, I supply fresh food whenever I can and yours is stale. I think Boo is a picky eater and prefers fresh food. The next time we are at the market, stock up on fresh food.~
@163  = ~But Minsc finds nothing wrong with food that is days old Nina. It tastes the same to me if I eat it the day it's bought or several days later.~
@164  = ~Minsc please get fresh food. Boo will be thankful for it right Boo? (Boo looks at Nina and shakes his head) See Minsc, Boo agrees.~
@165  = ~Ok, Minsc will keep fresh supplies of food with him from now on. Now hand Boo back over to Minsc.~
@166  = ~Boo is a cute fuzzy wuzzy, when he is not in Nina's food pouch. (Nina hands Boo over to Minsc.)~
@167  = ~Minsc you are wounded! You should get that wrapped up before an infection sets in.~
@168  = ~It is nothing but a little scratch, Nina. Minsc ain't got time to bleed.~
@169  = ~A scratch? You have blood pouring out like a water fountain!~
@170  = ~Boo seems to agree with you. He thinks it is best for Minsc to take Nina's advice. Plus Minsc feel a little woozy and lightheaded.~
@171  = ~Well you are lucky I have some wrappings in my pouch. I'll wrap it up for you if you want.~
@172  = ~Yes that would be best. Quiet Boo! Minsc hands not shake. I just caught a chill that's all.~
@173  = ~Stand still and let me get this on you and hold still. I don't want you bleeding all over me.~
@174  = ~I see you are a mage, Nalia, and very adept one at that. It pleases me to see that you use your magic wisely as well.~
@175  = ~I know magic quite well and I am also very good in the thieving arts. I do not do it for my own gain but to help those in need.~
@176  = ~Give to those in need? You sound similar to someone named Errol of the Hood.~
@177  = ~Errol of the Hood? Who was he, Nina?~
@178  = ~Errol of the Hood was a noble. He was also known as Errol Duke of Flynn. He was very rich and had vast amounts of lands until a rival neighbor set him up. He was accused of being a traitor to the king and his wealth and lands was taken from him. He eluded capture and started to recruit people to his cause. His merry band would steal from the rich and give to the poor.~
@179  = ~How interesting Nina. He sounds like the ideal noble knight in shining armor that I would like to meet.~
@180  = ~Umm well unfortunately he was caught and beheaded. But on the plus side, due to his popularity with the peasants they revolted against the tyrant king and the noble who set him up and they were disposed of.~
@181  = ~How heroic and noble of him. His sacrifice brought about the change to an unjust government and it's influences.~
@182  = ~Indeed it did. Hopefully it's something that will not happen to you. I think we will continue this story later.~
@183  = ~Valygar, have I done something to offend you? You keep staring at me with a look of suspion.~
@184  = ~I do not trust magic or those who use it. The power of magic corrupts a person's soul, it devastates those around them.~
@185  = ~I am not corrupted by magic, Valygar. I am humble servant of..~
@186  = ~Bah! You are no servant but a slave to magic. Its corrupting forces course in your body and you do its bidding.~
@187  = ~I am but a humble servant of Mystra and not a slave to anything or anyone. I use magic for helping people, not for my own personal gains. Your ignorance is most disturbing Valygar.~
@188  = ~It is not ignorance that I speak from, but knowledge of it personally.~
@189  = ~Personally? What was it that made you this way?~
@190  = ~I, I do not wish to discuss it. Just keep that foul magic far from me.~
@191  = ~Why do you keep staring at me, Ninafer? Have you never seen a sexy drow before or are you not used to one of your betters near you?~
@192  = ~I was debating where that foul stench was coming from, now I know it's from you. Do you filthy drow believe in bathing the dirt off your foul bodies or is that your natural putrid body odor?~
@193  = ~You amaze me "surface elf" I did not expect such a childish taunt from you. I was expecting something better but I was mistaken. A drow newborn can come up with something more insulting than that.~
@194  = ~(Nina smiles.) You will not provoke me "drow" so stop trying. I am looking at you because I am wondering what <CHARNAME> sees in you. I am curious as to why <PRO_HESHE> considers you a friend. I'd prefer seeing you burned at the stake than having you rescued, to tell the truth.~
@195  = ~Perhaps it's my natural good looks, my many talents or maybe I am more useful to <HIMHER> than you are.~
@196  = ~Useful on your back perhaps, but I don't think <CHARNAME> enlisted you for that. It must be because of your clerical powers that Shar grants you. Even if you were not a drow I still would consider you an enemy. Fear not, I will not kill you where you stand drow. I will how ever, watch you for signs of treachery and if I see anything, even the slightest, you will not know what hit you.~
@197  = ~If that is suppose to be a threat elf, I am not impressed. Do not worry about treachery from me, my loyalty is to <CHARNAME> only. By the way, you should keep both eyes on me, you never know when magic may stray in a fight and hit you.~
@198  = ~I have a question for you Anomen. How do you feel about being accepted into the Order of the Radiant Heart?~
@199  = ~It feels great Ninafer but I knew I would become a knight. I did not doubt it at all. I feel it's something I deserve after all. Simple, really.~
@200  = ~That sounds quite arrogant of you Anomen. What would happen if you failed your test, then where would you be?~
@201  = ~Nina, Nina, like I said failure was not an option with me. I excel at whatever task is laid before me and achieve my goal with little effort. Now if you are done discussing this with me, I have more important matters to occupy my time with.~
@202  = ~Oh trust me Ye Arrogant and Full of Himself I shall bother you no more now or in the future. People wonder why I do not join special knight orders? (Nina rambles to herself.)~
@203  = ~Ninafer, I would like to apologize for how I acted to you before. The excitement of becoming a knight with the Radiant Heart got the best of me. I acted in a very childish manner to you and I am sorry.~
@204  = ~Hey don't worry about it, Anomen. I can understand how the excitement can get to you.~
@205  = ~Yes is there something else, Anomen?~
@206  = ~Has anyone told you how beautiful your hair shines when the sunlight reflects off it? Or the way your eyes twinkle like the stars in the heavens?~
@207  = ~Ummm no not lately.~
@208  = ~Yes my lady it's quite true of what I said about you and more. I have never met such a fine looking elf like yourself. Mayhaps I can buy you a drink the next time we make a stop in a tavern?~
@209  = ~Uh that would be nice, Anomen, but I don't want you getting the wrong impression. I'm sure you're a nice guy but I am not interested in anything like that.~
@210  = ~My fair lady, you will be eating out of my hands soon enough. No one can resist my charms for very long.~
@211  = ~Well don't hold your breath, Mr. Full of Himself.~
@212  = ~Ah the sky has darken and far above the stars shine forth.~
@213  = ~Wish I may,
wish I might.
Upon a star that shines so bright.
Grant me a one wish this very night.~
@214  = ~What did you wish for Anomen?~
@215  = ~I am sorry my fair lady for I can't tell. If I did then it may not come true.~
@216  = ~Ok have it your way. Keep your secrets, I really don't care. (Nina gives Anomen a gentle push.)~
@217  = ~I think you do care my lady. I have a feeling this wish may come true after all.~
@218  = ~(Nina raises an eyebrow at his last comment.) Really? There is a saying that goes, "Be careful for what you wish for, for you may get it."~
@219  = ~Hey, Anomen, what do you have there?~
@220  = ~Nothing. (He quickly hides something in his pouch.)~
@221  = ~Nothing? Whatever it was you hid it quickly, it looked pretty shiny.~
@222  = ~Was it? I hadn't notice.~
@223  = ~Are you going to show me what it is or not?~
@224  = ~Some other time my lady.~
@225  = ~Fine, be that way about it. Play your little games, but remember, I can play them to.~
@226  = ~Oh what is this Anomen?~
@227  = ~(He hands Nina a small wrapped box.) A gift.~
@228  = ~(Nina unwraps the gift and takes out a coin.) A coin? An elven coin by the looks of the writing on it.~
@229  = ~It's my lucky coin. This coin came from Aryvandaar from what I have been told. Its been in my family for hundreds of generations.~
@230  = ~Aryvandaar? That was one of the old empires how did your family come across this?~
@231  = ~A great grandfather, was a wizard who was interested in elven lore and history. I guess he came across it in his travels.~
@232  = ~I can't take something like this, it must mean a lot to you. (Nina hands the coin back to Anomen.)~
@233  = ~(Anomen put the coin back in her soft hands and closes them.) Yes it does.~
@234  = ~(Anomen kisses Nina on the cheek.)~
@235  = ~(Anomen starts to walk away and Nina grabs a hold of him. She puts her lips to his and kisses him passionately.)~
@236  = ~(Realizing what she just did, she releases Anomen and quickly regains her composure.) Ah... well, we should get going. Yes that is it, get going, its all of a sudden become hot.~
@237  = ~Hey Anomen, um about that kiss we had...~
@238  = ~Are you going to give me another kiss from those moist soft lips of yours? (Anomen moves closer to Nina.)~
@239  = ~W-what? Ugh no, well maybe. Y-you're making me lose my, my focus. I was going to ask you...~
@240  = ~You're real sweet when you're flustered Nina.~
@241  = ~Flustered? I'm not flustered.~
@242  = ~Well you're stuttering and your face is turning red.~
@243  = ~Well it's red because of... of the heat.~
@244  = ~The heat? It doesn't feel that warm to me.~
@245  = ~Anomen, you are so frustrating at times!~
@246  = ~(Nina regains her composure.) I was going to ask if you enjoyed our last kiss, and if so, I was going to give you another. But you would rather make fun of me instead it appears, so I guess you will have to wait.~
@247  = ~(Anomen stands in front of Nina and leans his head down slightly in preparation of kissing Nina. Nina's breathing increases and she moves closer to greet his lips. Anomen pulls away at the last second.)~
@248  = ~I can wait, can you?~
@249  = ~Hey don't worry about it Anomen. I can understand how the excitement got to you.~
@250  = ~Thank you for being understanding. A knight does not act in a manner like that. To answer your original question I am very pleased and thankful that I became a knight. I worked long and hard for it.~
@251  = ~It is good that you achieved your goal Anomen and I am happy for you. A little bit of blood, sweat and tears will usually bring in a just reward.~
@252  = ~I wonder if <CHARNAME> is happy for you? I bet she is pleased by your admittance into the Order.~
@253  = ~My lady, is happy for me. She has been by my side since the trials began and has helped me on them. For this I am grateful to her.~
@254  = ~I am happy for the both of you. The two of you make a good couple. There is... well never mind, we should get going. We can talk more on this later as things progress between you two.~
@255  = ~Anomen, I think we need to talk. (She motions Anomen to come by her, away from <CHARNAME>'s hearing.)~
@256  = ~Yes, Nina, what is it?~
@257  = ~It's about our last talk, that I did not finish about you and <CHARNAME>. You two must stay focused on the task at hand. The upcoming days will be hard for her and you as well. We will be going against a very powerful mage and his minions. I would dread the thought of losing either one of you. I know you care about each other, but staying focused on the task at hand is of utmost importance.~
@258  = ~Worry not, Nina, no harm will ever come to <CHARNAME> while I still breathe. (Nina gives Anomen a questioning look.) Or myself either. We are focused on what is to come, so worry not.~
@259  = ~That's good to hear, Anomen. The two of you, well, have become my friends and I worry too much I guess. Things will be fine, you are right.~
@260  = ~Anomen I am sorry you did not become a knight. It is unfortunate that...~
@261  = ~I no longer care about the Order and their lies! I slaved for many years to become one of them and they throw me away like common refuse!~
@262  = ~Anomen, I know you are upset but the Order is a noble organization that only a select few can belong to.~
@263  = ~Yes, yes and it would appear I am not one of those precious "selected few". Begone from my sight! I no longer wish to discuss this!~
@264  = ~Alright girly ye won't know what hit ya!~
@265  = ~Ok you two that's enough! I will not have any fighting in my party.~
@266  = ~The bloody wench started it and I aim to end it!~
@267  = ~I saw what happened and she did not start it. She did not hit you with any of her spells, Korgan, so stop trying to start something. If you want to remain in MY group then this will stop! Understand?~
@268  = ~Fine! I'll do as ye wish fer now but I ain't forgettin this either.~
@269  = ~ And Nina needs to stop antagonizing Korgan, right, Nina?~
